Package: pkgexec
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Recommends: polkitd | policykit-1
Description: privileged per-verb apt effector for the Runix mutation boundary
 pkgexec is the privileged apt effector for Runix: nine per-verb libapt-pkg
 binaries that commit apt package transactions under pkexec/polkit and a
 broker-issued effect receipt.
 .
 Each apt verb (update, install, remove, purge, upgrade, dist_upgrade, configure,
 hold, unhold) is a distinct immutable entrypoint bound to its own polkit action;
 the verb is fixed by which binary path pkexec invoked, never by an argument. Only
 apt.update and apt.hold are authorized non-interactively, and only for members of
 the empty runix-apt-autonomous system group created by this package. The helper
 commits only after redeeming a single-use broker effect receipt whose plan digest
 matches the transaction it resolves under the held dpkg lock.
